  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Thursday) \n\nNevada will be located between a weak trough to the south, and a \nridge of high pressure strengthening to the north. The upper levels \nwill still remain dry from the overlying ridge, resulting in minimal \ncloud cover for the next few days. Unseasonably warm weather will \npersist through at least the weekend. High temperatures will be in \nthe upper 60s to lower 70s as we move into the weekend. Low \ntemperatures are currently expected to stay in the low 30s tonight \nand are expected to increase up to the upper 30s to lower 40s as we \nget to Sunday before the weather pattern shifts. \n\nAfter Monday, we are still expecting a polar jet to push through, \nbringing a very deep low, colder temperatures, and precipitation. \nLong range model guidance is showing a deep low moving off the \nPacific Ocean across portions of AZ, CA, and southern NV, which will \nextend a vorticity maxima line across the state with the passage.\nThe different models are still struggling with timing, but there\nis an overall trend of moving it later into the forecast period.\nThe GFS currently has the primary passage occurring for the\nTuesday into Wednesday time frame, while the ECMWF is looking more\nmid-day Thursday into Friday. Precipitation types are still a \nquestion, with the biggest concerns being around the surface. As of \nright now, the less whimsical option appears more likely, in the \nsurface lows will stay above freezing until after the FROPA and the \nprecipitation has passed. This means widespread rain is in the \nforecast with potential for snow mostly in the higher elevations. \nThis does not mean that we won\u2019t see any snow in the valleys, but \nthe likelihood of just rain is still seeming higher. As we push into \nthis event, the highs are supposed to be in the upper 50s/ low 60s \npre-frontal, and in the mid 40s/ low 50s post-frontal. The lows are \nexpected to follow the pattern of upper 30s/ low 40s pre-frontal, \nand in the mid 30s post-frontal. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence for a relatively \nclear and pleasant weekend. Medium confidence in the polar jet \nbringing precipitation and cold temperatures Tuesday through \nThursday. Low confidence in precipitation type and timing of the \npolar jet.",
